# Fixtures that are deliberately malformed.
#
# A hostile-input fixture has to stay exactly as written: its whole purpose is
# to be rejected by a parser, and several of them are not valid JSON or YAML at
# all. Prettier cannot parse such a file, so it reports an error and fails the
# whole format:check run rather than reporting a style difference. Listing them
# here keeps the check meaningful for the code around them.
#
# New hostile fixtures SHOULD use a `.malformed.` infix (for example
# `oversized.malformed.json`) so they are ignored by the pattern below without
# a further edit here. Only add an explicit path when a fixture cannot follow
# that convention.

tests/connectors/fixtures/**/*.malformed.*
tests/connectors/fixtures/import/canary-invalid.json
